Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["P3HT / O-IDTBR Charge-Transfer Exciton Model", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"6c9d4067-8e4b-41c3-8654-2688933d626e"],

Cell["\<\
Companion code for: Jindal, Janik & Milner, \"First-Principles Modeling of \
Interfacial Charge Transfer Exciton States in Organic Solar Cells\" (JCTC).\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"3848cb4a-d858-4b8b-84f7-f899f1f6e42b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Overview", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9a2191ba-645e-4f4a-a4a8-ef2d1838f721"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook orchestrates the full calculation of charge-transfer (CT) \
exciton energies at a P3HT / O-IDTBR donor-acceptor interface, using a \
tight-binding model parameterized from DFT and applied to close-contact \
geometries taken from a molecular dynamics trajectory.

The total CT exciton energy is E_CT = E_K + E_C + E_P, i.e. the one-body \
kinetic energy of the delocalized electron and hole (E_K), the electron-hole \
Coulomb interaction (E_C), and the dielectric polarization stabilization \
(E_P) (Eq. 2 and Eq. 12 of the paper).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.994449398698053*^9, 
  3.994449403697804*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"54a8857d-5524-49b1-91f3-\
6f9c0283f99b"],

Cell["Evaluate sections in order from top to bottom. ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996000000000001*^9, 
  3.994449331006658*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"73344a9e-4e5c-4c55-b3bc-\
860ada13462d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"SetDirectory", "[", 
  RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.88834007684976*^9, 3.888340082208136*^9}, {
  3.994449419597066*^9, 
  3.994449420641842*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3e791500-d63f-4450-aa70-\
471f914676cb"]
}, Open  ]],

